File Index

/MapPage.test.tsx
Purpose: MapPage tests — first area renders rooms + portal stub, room click hands off a room ref to onOpenRoom, portal click fetches and renders the neighboring area's map in place; Phase 13 spawn overlay: off-by-default (no /spawn fetch), toggle on renders per-room mob-count badges (object-only rooms excluded) + legend entry, toggle off hides them. Phase 14b scaffolding: "Edit exits" toggle (area mode only, hidden in world mode) fetches the full AreaFile via api.getArea and renders THAT (not the /api/map projection — proven by a fixture that differs between the two), Spawns checkbox force-disables while editing, toggling back off with no staged ops needs no confirm. Phase 14b drag-to-connect: pointerDown room A + pointerUp room B opens the create-exit popover with the grid-inferred direction, dropping on the source room itself cancels, Create stages an addExit op (staged-count badge + new rendered edge) while Cancel stages nothing, Escape cancels an in-progress drag (ghost line gone), the Enter/Enter keyboard path opens the same popover, and background pointerdown/up on the canvas never opens it (pan is unaffected). Phase 14b edge popover + tray: clicking an existing two-way edge opens the edit popover prefilled from the CURRENT exit (lock state, key vnum) with the also-remove-reverse checkbox offered (reverse genuinely points back here), Update stages an updateExit op visible in the tray list, Delete+alsoReverse removes both sides from the rendered layout, per-item tray undo restores it, Discard all clears every staged op. Phase 14b save pipeline: Save previews (PreviewPane diff shown) before saving, Confirm clears ops/refetches both the AreaFile and the map projection/toasts success, Cancel leaves ops staged and never PUTs; a 401 surfaces the client's own "Access tab" guard message with ops left intact; a 409 renders the reused ConflictPanel — Reload discards staged ops after a confirm() and refetches, Save anyway PUTs the STAGED (edited) model with no baseHash.

/MapPage.tsx
Purpose: Map tab (Phase 12) — SVG area map from /api/map/:file: rooms on the BFS grid (click → Areas tab via areaTarget lift), classification-aware exit edges (Phase 12b: arrowheads for one-way, dashed red non-returning, self-loop rings, amber door markers with lock-state titles, dotted violet script-warp edges) + an HTML legend, dashed portal stubs for cross-area exits/warps (click → that area's map), drag-pan/wheel-zoom viewBox, area picker + Area/World mode toggle; Phase 13: "Spawns" toolbar toggle fetches /api/areas/:file/spawn (only while on) and overlays green top-left mob-count badges on room nodes. Phase 14b: opt-in "Edit exits" toggle fetches the full AreaFile (api.getArea) and stages edits as an ExitOp list (exit-edit.ts) replayed into an editLayout via the SAME layoutArea/AreaMapSvg as view mode; area/mode switches and the edit-off toggle confirm-guard discard of staged ops (window.confirm) via guardDiscard; Spawns force-disabled while editing. Drag-to-connect: pointerdown on a room (stopPropagation so the pan handler never sees it) starts a ghost line tracked in SVG coords via clientToSvg, dropping on another room opens an HTML create-exit popover (direction/two-way/lock-state/key, prefilled via inferDirection) positioned over the SVG (not inside it — a wrapping .mb-map-canvas div), Escape cancels at any stage; an Enter-arm/Enter-connect keyboard path mirrors the same flow for a11y. Confirm calls onCreateExit → MapPage pushes an addExit op. Edge popover: clicking an internal/external edge (never warp — those are script-derived, not RoomExit records) resolves the full RoomExit via a resolveExit prop (reads editedArea directly — LayoutEdge doesn't carry key) and opens a read-only cross-area note or an editable lock-state/key form with Update (→ onUpdateExit) and Delete (→ onRemoveExit, "also remove reverse" gated on classification==='two-way' so it's only offered when applyOps would actually act on it); editLayout now also threads a resolveExternal oracle sourced from the last /api/map fetch (`data`) through areaToMapRooms so an EXISTING cross-area exit still renders as a portal stub in edit mode (a newly staged one stays dangling — creation is out of scope). Staged-changes tray (docked under the legend): one line per op via describeOp, per-item ✕ undo (drop + re-replay), Discard all, and a Save button badged with the op count. Save pipeline reuses the AreasPage precedent exactly: api.preview → PreviewPane (imported straight from features/areas) + Confirm/Cancel → api.save(file, editedArea, baseHash); success clears ops and re-pulls BOTH api.getArea and api.areaMap (refetchAfterSave) so edit mode and view mode both reflect the just-written disk state; 409 → the shared ConflictPanel (features/areas/workbench.js) with Reload (confirm → discard ops, refetch) / Save-anyway (confirm → unconditional PUT of the staged model); other errors (incl. 401, whose "— set your builder token in the Access tab" suffix is added by client.ts's request() itself) surface via a toast with ops left intact. View mode itself remains behavior-identical/read-only.

/exit-edit.test.ts
Purpose: exit-edit unit tests — addExit two-way both-sides + occupied-reverse/non-local-target one-way downgrade warnings, locks/key carried onto both sides, updateExit patch + missing-exit warning, removeExit forward-only vs alsoReverse (incl. mismatched-reverse warning), replay determinism (same ops twice = same result), inferDirection all 8 compass sectors + zero-delta default + shallow-diagonal snapping (never up/down), areaToMapRooms projection (drops non-exit fields, never sets `external` unless the optional resolver matches), describeOp room-name formatting.

/exit-edit.ts
Purpose: Pure staged-edit engine for the Phase 14b map exit editor (client-local, zero React) — ExitOp union (addExit/updateExit/removeExit) + applyOps immutable replay over the #ROOMS section of an AreaFile (per-item undo = drop the op, re-replay); two-way adds mirror REV_DIR and downgrade to one-way + warning when the reverse slot is occupied or the target room isn't local; inferDirection snaps a grid delta to the nearest of the 8 compass doors (never up/down); areaToMapRooms projects the edited AreaFile back into AreaMapRoom[] for layoutArea (layout.ts) — takes an optional `resolveExternal(from,door,to)` oracle (MapPage wires it to the last /api/map fetch) so an existing cross-area exit can still render as a portal stub in edit mode; without a match (or the resolver omitted) the exit stays dangling — no edge — same as before; describeOp renders a tray-ready summary line.

/WorldMap.test.tsx
Purpose: WorldMap tests — nodes for all areas incl. broken flagged, link tooltip lists the connecting exit, node click calls onOpenArea.

/WorldMap.tsx
Purpose: World-level map (Phase 12) — every area.lst entry as a circle node (radius by room count, broken files dashed red), directional cross-area exit links as edges (thickness by count, hover title lists each connecting exit), node click drills into the area map.

/layout.test.ts
Purpose: layoutArea unit tests — linear east corridor on one row, N/E/S/W loop closes onto a 2x2 square, collision never stacks two rooms, disconnected components don't overlap, external exit → portal + external edge while dangling exits are skipped.

/layout.ts
Purpose: Pure BFS grid layout (no deps): 10-direction door deltas (Phase 12b — diagonals own the corner cells, U/D ring-placed near the source), per-component BFS from the lowest vnum with components stacked vertically, collision probe along the direction then ring fallback, REV_DIR-based exit classification (two-way/one-way/non-returning/loop) with locks carried onto edges, warp edges + warp portal stubs, dangling exits drawn as nothing; normalized to a (0,0) origin.

/map.css
Purpose: Map tab styles — mode toggle, SVG canvas (grab cursor), room/portal node + edge classes (external dashed amber; Phase 12b: one-way/non-returning/warp/loop edge variants, arrowheads, rotated door marker, legend swatches; Phase 13: spawn toggle, green spawn badge, spawn legend swatch), world node/link classes with broken-state variant.
